[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Collecting]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.33]Lesson 59 | 第59课
[00:02.40]Collecting | 收藏
[00:08.71]What in particular does a person gain when he or she becomes a serious collector? | 一个人成为认真的收藏家之后，特别能得到什么？
[00:17.12]People tend to amass possessions, sometimes without being aware of doing so. | 人们倾向于积攒财物，有时并没有意识到自己在这样做。
[00:22.96]Indeed they can have a delightful surprise when they find something useful which they did not know they owned. | 的确，当他们发现自己拥有某件有用的、但先前并不知道自己有的东西时，会惊喜万分。
[00:30.68]Those who never have to move house become indiscriminate collectors of what can only be described as clutter. | 那些从来不必搬家的人成了不加区别的收藏家，收藏的只能被称作杂物。
[00:38.27]They leave unwanted objects in drawers, cupboards and attics for years, in the belief that they may one day need just those very things. | 他们把无用的东西在抽屉、碗柜和顶楼里一放就是好几年，相信总有一天会正好用上这些东西。
[00:48.40]As they grow old, people also accumulate belongings for two other reasons, | 随着年龄的增长，人们还因另外两个原因积攒物品：
[00:54.85]lack of physical and mental energy, both of which are essential in turning out and throwing away, and sentiment. | 缺乏体力和精力——这两者对清理和丢弃东西都是必不可少的——以及感情上的依恋。
[01:03.55]Things owned for a long time are full of associations with the past, | 长期拥有的物品充满对过去的联想，
[01:08.41]perhaps with relatives who are dead, and so they gradually acquire a value beyond their true worth. | 也许与已经去世的亲人有关，因此逐渐获得了超出其真实价值的价值。
[01:16.11]Some things are collected deliberately in the home in an attempt to avoid waste. | 有些东西是有意收集在家里的，为了避免浪费。
[01:21.49]Among these I would list string and brown paper, | 在这些东西中，我会列举绳子和牛皮纸，
[01:24.50]kept by thrifty people when a parcel has been opened, to save buying these two requisites. | 节俭的人在包裹拆开之后留着它们，省得再买这两样必需品。
[01:31.45]Collecting small items can easily become a mania. | 收集小物品很容易成为一种癖好。
[01:35.57]I know someone who always cuts sketches out from newspapers of model clothes that she would like to buy if she had the money. | 我认识一个人，她总是从报纸上剪下她有钱就会买的时装式样的图片。
[01:43.88]As she is not rich, the chances that she will ever be able to afford such purchases are remote; | 由于她并不富有，她能买得起这些东西的可能性微乎其微，
[01:51.93]but she is never sufficiently strongminded to be able to stop the practice. | 但她永远不能下定决心停止这种做法。
[01:57.24]It is a harmless habit, but it litters up her desk to such an extent that every time she opens it, loose bits of paper fall out in every direction. | 这是一种无害的习惯，但它把她的写字台塞得满满的，以致每次打开抽屉，碎纸片便向四面八方散落。
[02:09.31]Collecting as a serious hobby is quite different and has many advantages. | 把收藏作为一种认真的爱好则完全不同，有许多好处。
[02:15.15]It provides relaxation for leisure hours, as just looking at one's treasures is always a joy. | 它为闲暇时光提供放松，因为光是看看自己的珍藏就是一种乐趣。
[02:22.72]One does not have to go outside for amusement, since the collection is housed at home. | 人们不必到外面去寻求消遣，因为收藏品就存放在家里。
[02:28.80]Whatever it consists of, stamps, records, first editions of books, china, glass, | 无论收藏的是什么——邮票、唱片、初版书、瓷器、玻璃器皿、
[02:37.08]antique furniture, pictures, model cars, stuffed birds, toy animals, there is always something to do in connection with it, | 古董家具、绘画、模型汽车、鸟类标本、玩具动物——总与之有关的事情可做，
[02:47.44]from finding the right place for the latest addition, to verifying facts in reference books. | 从为最新的藏品寻找合适的存放位置，到在参考书中核实事实。
[02:53.67]This hobby educates one not only in the chosen subject, but also in general matters which have some bearing on it. | 这种爱好不仅使人在选定的科目上受教育，而且在与之有关的一般事务上也受教育。
[03:02.06]There are also other benefits. | 还有其他好处。
[03:04.94]One wants to meet like-minded collectors, to get advice, to compare notes, to exchange articles, to show off the latest find. | 人们想结识志同道合的收藏家，征求意见、交流心得、交换藏品、炫耀最新的收获。
[03:14.33]So one's circle of friends grows. | 于是朋友圈子扩大了。
[03:17.07]Soon the hobby leads to travel, perhaps to a meeting in another town, | 不久，这种爱好便带来了旅行，也许去另一个城市参加聚会，
[03:22.50]possibly a trip abroad in search of a rare specimen, for collectors are not confined to any one country. | 或许到国外寻找一件珍品，因为收藏家不局限于任何一个国家。
[03:30.33]Over the years, one may well become an authority on one's hobby and will very probably be asked to give informal talks to little gatherings | 多年之后，一个人很可能会成为自己爱好方面的权威，并且很可能被邀请给小型聚会作非正式的讲话，
[03:40.08]and then, if successful, to larger audiences. | 如果成功的话，再面对更多的听众。
[03:44.84]In this way self-confidence grows, first from mastering a subject, then from being able to talk about it. | 就这样，自信心增强了，先是来自掌握一门学问，然后来自能够谈论它。
[03:53.93]Collecting, by occupying spare time so constructively, makes a person contented, with no time for boredom. | 收藏通过如此富有建设性地占用闲暇时间，使人感到满足，没有时间感到无聊。
